SUMMARY:(1633) Chimay hides a mag 11.5 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(1633) Chimay hides a magnitude 11.5 star\, seen from Etawah.\n
 The predicted edge passes 17 km to the SSE\, so a miss is likely — but a
  chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nCloses
 t approach 23:45:03 IST\, give or take 1 s. The star is 51° up in the S 
 · dark sky.\nIt fades 4.1 magnitudes for up to 2.6 s on the centre line\,
  and the path is 37 km wide\, give or take 36 km.\nFinder chart\, the map 
 and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2027-08#2027-08-29
